 "notes": "Dark photon dark matter coupled to baryon number B (abstract: coupled to baryons; L=-eps*e*J^mu A_mu, Eq.2, J^mu = baryon or B-L current). Kinetic-mixing DP is explicitly stated as future work, so this is a U(1)_B(-L)-type vector boson, reported in the VectorBL g_BL plane. Curve from Fig.5 (ep figure semi_full_all_upper_limits.png), the fully-coherent matched-filter limit (red=low-frequency + black=high-frequency), taking the lower envelope (best reach) of the excluded region as the exclusion boundary. Y-axis of the figure is eps^2_95%; reported values are eps = sqrt(eps^2) (never eps^2). eps is the coupling normalized to the electromagnetic charge e; I report eps DIRECTLY as g_BL (i.e. no extra x e factor applied) consistent with the plotted quantity. The stochastic O(1) correction increasing eps^2 by a factor of 9 is already applied in Fig.5. Mass range ~9e-20 to 1.15e-14 eV/c2 (frequency [2e-5,5] Hz). Semi-coherent (magenta) result is a less sensitive alternative and is not reported. Paper assumes local rho_DM in Eq.4 but does not quote a numeric value (v0=220 km/s virial velocity), so dm_density_assumed is null; limit scales as rho_DM^-1/2. CL=95%.",
